## 4. Dataset Coverage and Analytical Scope

The five datasets represent different dimensions of hospital performance.

| Performance Domain | Analytical Focus |
|---|---|
| Total Performance Score | Overall hospital performance |
| Clinical Outcomes | Clinical quality and patient outcomes |
| Person and Community Engagement | Patient experience and satisfaction |
| Safety | Patient safety and healthcare-associated complications |
| Efficiency | Efficiency and Medicare spending measures |

The consolidated dataset provides a common hospital-level structure for comparing performance across these domains.

## 5. Data Integration and Preparation

The source datasets were brought together using the hospital facility identifier and fiscal year.

The preparation process included:

- Inspection of original source datasets.
- Standardisation of column names and data formats.
- Validation of hospital identifiers.
- Handling of missing and unavailable values.
- Integration of the five datasets.
- Verification of record counts and score consistency.
- Preparation of the consolidated analytical dataset.

The original published datasets are distinguished from the cleaned, transformed and analytical outputs created during this project.

## 6. Data Quality and Validation

Data quality checks were performed to improve the reliability of the consolidated dataset.

Key validation activities included:

- Checking duplicate and missing records.
- Verifying hospital identifiers.
- Reviewing domain score availability.
- Comparing weighted domain scores with the Total Performance Score.
- Checking consistency across the integrated datasets.

These checks supported the subsequent Excel, SQL Server, Power BI, Tableau and statistical analyses.

